{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1249401-fae-cunning-and-weapons","id":1249401,"title":"Fae Cunning and Weapons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-28T07:35:31-07:00","id":1249401,"title":"Fae Cunning and Weapons","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tinos\">I got an interesting question from one of my players about Fae Cunning that I was looking to get additional input on. The question comes down to what happens after you you use the second part of the contract and, after a successful dodge, redirect the attack at a valid target. If the person swinging is using a weapon should the damage be equal to the Changeling's presence, or the Changeling's presence + the weapon modifier? I've previously been running that a re-directed attack gains the damage type of the original swing, so someone with lethal mein or the beast seeming blessing will do lethal to themselves if they were swinging with lethal, and that ruling implies that weapon modifier should be added. The issue to me is that this comes after a dodge action, which often gets to fairly high pools, and then applies automatic successes. A high presence changeling with a decent defense pool facing down someone with an average weapon can easily be dealing 8 lethal in a turn.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tinos\">This just seems a bit strong, particularly for a Common contract. I think it's about on par with the Aggravated damage done with Talon and Wing plus Beast Seeming/Lethal Mein, but that one requires a Royal Contract plus a Seeming or Merit to accomplish. Does anyone else have opinions on this?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tinos\">Additionally, what would most people consider 'valid targets' in reference to Fae Cunning? I've been figuring that the attack can be redirected back at the attacker in melee, but I would rule that in a firefight the attacker is not valid. Other things behind the Changeling using the contract would be, but anything coming from the direction of the attack would not.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24249-muattles","name":"Muattles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T07:43:05-07:00","id":1249407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muattles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1249401-fae-cunning-and-weapons#post1249401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, what would most people consider 'valid targets' in reference to Fae Cunning? I've been figuring that the attack can be redirected back at the attacker in melee, but I would rule that in a firefight the attacker is not valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like the exact opposite of how those forms of attack work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T10:17:54-07:00","id":1249466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1249401-fae-cunning-and-weapons?p=1249407#post1249407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like the exact opposite of how those forms of attack work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I...don't quite follow what you mean? If a melee attacker comes up and swings at someone with a sword or with their fists, it makes sense that Fae Cunning might redirect the attack back at that person in the same way some martial arts can use an attacker's momentum against them and hurt the attacker. These attacks could also of course be redirected at other targets, such as the attackers friends two feet behind the Changeling, but I would say the attacker is a 'valid target'.<br /> <br /> In a firefight there isn't really a way for a bullet to pull a full 180 and shoot the person who fired it. This is supernatural magic we're talking about here, but I figure the contract is already giving the Changeling defense against Firearms, which normally doesn't apply, so I don't need to beef it up further and allow for attacks to be redirected back at the shooter. Again, if the attack is redirected to shoot the attackers friend a couple feet behind the Changeling, that is valid in my mind.<br /> <br /> What is your interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24249-muattles","name":"Muattles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T10:49:39-07:00","id":1249484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muattles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1249401-fae-cunning-and-weapons?p=1249466#post1249466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I...don't quite follow what you mean? If a melee attacker comes up and swings at someone with a sword or with their fists, it makes sense that Fae Cunning might redirect the attack back at that person in the same way some martial arts can use an attacker's momentum against them and hurt the attacker.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't just using the attacker's momentum to make them hurt themselves \u2014 it's <i>redirecting the attack</i>, which makes less visual sense for melee attacks unless you're operating under the assumption that Fae Cunning is working on the principle of Stop Hitting Yourself. Ricochets and wild shots, meanwhile, are a known phenomenon in the narrative quiver of ranged attacks.<br /> <br /> That being said, I think the intention is that you're redirecting the attack to a third party or piece of scenery regardless of type, not reflecting it back as a matter of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-28-2018, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}